"stage19_causal_queue":"1969-05-01"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11467","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"SECTION 1. The Secretary of State is hereby designated and empowered to perform the following-described functions without the approval, ratification, or other action of the President:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"a2dd2bda47ef89b6a2b53efe01b359bccc4827f509e72d006469c9448354cb7e","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-11467-delegating-the-secretary-state-authority-approve-or-reject"},"scope_id":"EO:11467#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) The authority vested in the President by section 6(a) of the North Pacific Fisheries Act of 1954 (68 Stat. 699; 16 U.S.C. 1025 (a)) to accept or reject, on behalf of the United States, recommendations made by the International North Pacific Fisheries Commission in accordance with the provisions of Article III, section 1, of the International Convention for the High Seas Fisheries of the North Pacific Ocean (signed at Tokyo May 9, 1952, TIAS 2786) and recommendations made by the Commission in pursuance of the provisions of the Protocol to that Convention.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 1(1)","sha256":"a2dd2bda47ef89b6a2b53efe01b359bccc4827f509e72d006469c9448354cb7e","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-11467-delegating-the-secretary-state-authority-approve-or-reject"},"scope_id":"EO:11467#sec1(1)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(2) The authority vested in the President by Article III, paragraph 2, of the Convention between the United States of America and Canada for the Preservation of the Halibut Fishery of the Northern Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea (signed at Ottawa, March 2, 1953, TIAS 2900) to approve or reject actions of the International Pacific Halibut Commission taken pursuant to that paragraph.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 1(2)","sha256":"a2dd2bda47ef89b6a2b53efe01b359bccc4827f509e72d006469c9448354cb7e","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-11467-delegating-the-secretary-state-authority-approve-or-reject"},"scope_id":"EO:11467#sec1(2)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"SEC. 2. In carrying out his authority under section 1 of this order the Secretary of State shall consult with the Secretary of the Interior.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); Sec. 2","sha256":"a2dd2bda47ef89b6a2b53efe01b359bccc4827f509e72d006469c9448354cb7e","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-11467-delegating-the-secretary-state-authority-approve-or-reject"},"scope_id":"EO:11467#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"34 FR 7271, PDF pages 5-5","sha256":"85368b6ac081d7a03f208f64d443fd356ee4616fbe27caf600a1d380cb3f052c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1969-05-03/pdf/FR-1969-05-03.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 4 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine 